@model PetBox.Web.Pages.Shared.ObservationSignalModel
@* spec observation-regression-signalled-on-card: "we fixed it and it came back" is the highest-
   value signal the whole observation mechanism exists to surface (work
   observation-recurrence-after-fix-signal) — a SEPARATE, noticeable alert banner, deliberately
   NOT another badge sharing the row with the plain recurrence counter (_ObservationRecurrenceBadge).
   Uses the project's standard alert-warning convention (doc/ui-conventions.md).
   live-verification finding (2026-08-28, owner screenshot on `observations/live3-prov-check-
   cache-evict`): this used to always link through the opaque Routes.TaskBoardNode(id) route,
   showing the raw 32-hex NodeId as link text ("fixed by 65ce101c2a864c04b32869675ce2f30d") — PetBox
   addresses by either NodeId or slug, but the UI convention prefers a slug (the SAME exhaustive
   relations panel lower on this page already resolves its targets to a slug when it can). Now
   renders the slug when the caller resolved one (Model.FixedByLink, built via
   ObservationFixedByResolver — the SAME ITasksService.GetNodeAsync door the relations panel's own
   LinkRef reaches through, not a second path); degrades to the raw NodeId, never fails to render,
   when the target is unresolved/missing (Model.FixedByLink is null or its Status is "missing").
   live-verification finding (2026-08-28, owner screenshot): the bare U+26A0 WARNING SIGN glyph
   used to render with its default COLOR-EMOJI presentation (most platforms ship it pre-coloured
   orange/yellow-on-triangle), which all but disappeared against this alert's own warning-yellow
   fill — the banner TEXT already contrasts correctly (daisyUI's alert-warning sets the text colour
   per theme; that part was never broken), only the emoji's own baked-in fill fought the background.
   The fix forces TEXT presentation via the U+FE0E variation selector, which makes browsers render
   a plain monochrome glyph that inherits `color` like any other character — the SAME
   already-correct warning-on-warning-background text colour every other word in this banner
   already uses, in every theme (dark/light/nord/retro — daisyUI computes the pairing per theme,
   this glyph now just rides it instead of overriding it with its own colour). No new colour or
   class introduced; the icon is decorative (the adjacent text already states "recurred after
   fix"), so it's aria-hidden. *@
@if (Model.Observation is { RecurredAfterFixAt: { } regressedAt } o)
{
	<div class="alert alert-warning text-xs py-1.5 px-2 mt-1" data-testid="node-observation-regression" role="alert">
		<span><span aria-hidden="true">⚠︎</span> recurred after fix — <time class="local-time" datetime="@regressedAt.ToString("o")" data-testid="node-observation-regressed-at">@regressedAt.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm")</time></span>
		@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(o.FixedByNodeId))
		{
			@if (Model.FixedByLink is { Status: not "missing" } l && l is { Board: { Length: > 0 } b, Slug: { Length: > 0 } s })
			{
				<a href="@Routes.TaskBoardNodeBySlug(Model.WorkspaceKey, Model.ProjectKey, b, s)" class="link link-hover font-mono" data-testid="node-observation-fixed-by-link">fixed by @s</a>
			}
			else
			{
				<a href="@Routes.TaskBoardNode(Model.WorkspaceKey, Model.ProjectKey, o.FixedByNodeId)" class="link link-hover font-mono" data-testid="node-observation-fixed-by-link">fixed by @o.FixedByNodeId</a>
			}
		}
	</div>
}
